; input_slot_out_of_range: INPUT addressing a calldata slot the host did
; not fix raises CallDataIndex rather than storing a null.
;
; spec/xqvm/ISA.md's INPUT row states that the host fixes the calldata
; before the run and that a slot outside [0, slots) is a program error
; rather than a null result. The bound is the slot count: an in-range slot
; the host left unset is a different case and reads as unset, which
; calldata_hole_reads_as_unset pins.
;
; A VM that returned None with no bounds check would charge nothing, store
; None in r0, and halt successfully -- a fault-versus-success error
; against the spec text.

PUSH 0
INPUT r0         ; calldata is empty, so slot 0 does not exist
HALT
